We've talked about this and decided:

1. We should disable the update checker in our official Debian and RPM packages;
2. We should cancel the update checker goroutine if the main command finishes beforehand, so that the checker cannot ever delay the exit status of the command;
3. We could consider dropping the entire update checker functionality altogether. It was primarily added because we found out that Homebrew users were often running an extremely out-of-date version. https://github.com/Homebrew/homebrew-core/blob/6e18df78b5e501501106a8f2477d4ee75e5c2dfe/Formula/gh.rb#L30
